{"duration_api_ms":41759,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c092474b-b4e0-47b3-ae8e-7b81d4e4d476","total_cost_usd":0.19797579999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11032,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"output_tokens":5471,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2395},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11032,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5471,"cache_read_input_tokens":1459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11032},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5471,"cacheReadInputTokens":1459,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11032,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.19797579999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2395,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"merged_document\":\"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\\n\\nIt consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can later be used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\n\\nThis BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\\n\\n## Motivation\\n\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription. It is not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the mnemonic\\n\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. With more entropy security is improved but the sentence length increases. We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\"decisions\":[{\"slot\":\"title\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"# BIP: 39\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"# BIP: 39\",\"reason\":\"Base document's title; the other document carries only a section heading.\"},{\"slot\":\"placement of mnemonic generation section\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"## Generating the memonic\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"## Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"Placed after Motivation as a new section; base has no slot for it.\"}],\"dispositions\":[{\"segment\":\"a3\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected 'letters' to 'words' and 'UTOXs' to 'wallets'.\"},{\"segment\":\"a4\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected 'ASCII seed' to 'binary seed'.\"},{\"segment\":\"a5\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This seed can later be used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\",\"reason\":\"Word order fixed: 'can be later' to 'can later be'.\"},{\"segment\":\"a7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected licence from GPL to 2-clause BSD.\"},{\"segment\":\"a9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected 'wallet satoshis' to 'wallet seed'.\"},{\"segment\":\"a11\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected 'determinism' to 'randomness'.\"},{\"segment\":\"a12\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"It is not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\"reason\":\"Fixed typo 'süeed' and expanded contraction.\"},{\"segment\":\"b1\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"## Generating the mnemonic\",\"reason\":\"Fixed heading typo 'memonic'.\"},{\"segment\":\"b2\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\"reason\":\"Fixed 'demonic' typo and corrected 23 to 32 bits.\"},{\"segment\":\"b5\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected range to 128-256 bits, matching the table.\"},{\"segment\":\"b7\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected hash name SHA652 to SHA256.\"},{\"segment\":\"b8\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected 'start' to 'end'.\"},{\"segment\":\"b9\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\"reason\":\"Corrected group size 12 to 11 bits, matching the formula.\"}],\"mismatch\":\"\",\"additions\":[{\"statement\":\"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\"corrects\":\"a group of easy to remember letters -- for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39 mnemonics are words and it generates deterministic wallets.\"},{\"statement\":\"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\"corrects\":\"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39 derives a 512-bit binary seed via PBKDF2.\"},{\"statement\":\"This BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\",\"corrects\":\"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39's copyright section names the 2-clause BSD license.\"},{\"statement\":\"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\"corrects\":\"a wallet satoshis\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"The mnemonic represents a wallet seed, not satoshis.\"},{\"statement\":\"This guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated randomness with a human-readable transcription.\",\"corrects\":\"computer-generated determinism\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"The mnemonic transcribes generated entropy, i.e. randomness.\"},{\"statement\":\"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\"corrects\":\"a multiple of 23 bits\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"All ENT values in the table are multiples of 32; CS = ENT / 32.\"},{\"statement\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\"corrects\":\"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts.\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39 allows 128-256 bits, as the document's own table shows.\"},{\"statement\":\"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\"corrects\":\"SHA652\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39 uses SHA256; SHA652 does not exist.\"},{\"statement\":\"This checksum is appended to the end of the initial entropy.\",\"corrects\":\"appended to the start of the initial entropy\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"BIP-39 appends the checksum to the end of the entropy.\"},{\"statement\":\"Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 11 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist.\",\"corrects\":\"groups of 12 bits\",\"basis\":\"own-knowledge\",\"source\":\"\",\"reason\":\"0-2047 needs 11 bits and the table uses MS = (ENT + CS) / 11.\"}]}","ttft_ms":21545,"type":"result","duration_ms":41824,"uuid":"6161c0bb-9216-49f8-b01a-db8f20e322cc","ttft_stream_ms":1188,"time_to_request_ms":65,"first_content_frame_ms":1189,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
